      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research eliminating the per-iteration interior copy with two-buffer ping-pong updates. Optionally use contiguous row-major allocations to improve locality, but measure that separately from copy elimination. Preserve the stencil expression order, convergence test and iteration limit. Keep boundary values identical in both buffers, including any nonzero boundary cells from initialization; handle small grids and zero iterations. Preserve the existing output format, then report correctness and measured runtime against the baseline.\",\"B\":\"Research row-level parallelism for the stencil update using the existing compiler/toolchain. Use race-free writes and a per-iteration logical-OR reduction for the convergence flag; ensure every worker finishes before the next iteration or buffer swap. Keep output serialized and ordered. Measure parallel overhead and use a general workload-based cutoff if beneficial; do not tune to particular test cases or change the target or compiler.\",\"C\":\"Research an exact active-region optimization based on the source's fixed initialization: track a conservative bounding box containing all potentially nonzero cells and expand it by one cell per iteration, clipped to the grid. Cells outside it have zero neighbors, so their update and error are both zero; skip them only while that invariant is maintained. Include fixed boundary values in the initial bounds, preserve the exact convergence decision and final update, and fall back to a full sweep when the active region is no longer profitable. Validate across all supplied cases and measure the result.\",\"G\":\"Evaluate the A, B and C candidates independently for correctness and runtime using the unchanged test/oracle, compiler, budget and ARM64 target. Integrate only validated work; test promising combinations afresh rather than assuming gains add together, and retain the fastest correct measured version. Preserve the source's convergence and output behavior, and report integration measurements as well as the chosen candidate.\",\"analysis\":\"This is Problem E's Jacobi stencil. The baseline is valid on 4 cases, with mean runtime 0.06614 s (three samples: 0.06557–0.06693 s) and score 0.50 on a 4-core ARM64 target. No candidate measurements are present, so these are research hypotheses, not claimed gains. The source updates interior cells from four neighbors, stops only after a full iteration finds no change above 1e-5 or reaches the iteration limit, keeps initialized boundaries fixed, and prints every value with six decimals and a trailing space. Each objective must preserve those semantics for every valid input; the active-region proposal relies on the source's general initialization, not test-specific values.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"40733d785879d263e1ffc66992962bd8fde45b50b008634d85d368a534cb4715\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research eliminating the per-iteration interior copy with two-buffer ping-pong updates. Optionally use contiguous row-major allocations to improve locality, but measure that separately from copy elimination. Preserve the stencil expression order, convergence test and iteration limit. Keep boundary values identical in both buffers, including any nonzero boundary cells from initialization; handle small grids and zero iterations. Preserve the existing output format, then report correctness and measured runtime against the baseline.\",\"B\":\"Research row-level parallelism for the stencil update using the existing compiler/toolchain. Use race-free writes and a per-iteration logical-OR reduction for the convergence flag; ensure every worker finishes before the next iteration or buffer swap. Keep output serialized and ordered. Measure parallel overhead and use a general workload-based cutoff if beneficial; do not tune to particular test cases or change the target or compiler.\",\"C\":\"Research an exact active-region optimization based on the source's fixed initialization: track a conservative bounding box containing all potentially nonzero cells and expand it by one cell per iteration, clipped to the grid. Cells outside it have zero neighbors, so their update and error are both zero; skip them only while that invariant is maintained. Include fixed boundary values in the initial bounds, preserve the exact convergence decision and final update, and fall back to a full sweep when the active region is no longer profitable. Validate across all supplied cases and measure the result.\",\"G\":\"Evaluate the A, B and C candidates independently for correctness and runtime using the unchanged test/oracle, compiler, budget and ARM64 target. Integrate only validated work; test promising combinations afresh rather than assuming gains add together, and retain the fastest correct measured version. Preserve the source's convergence and output behavior, and report integration measurements as well as the chosen candidate.\",\"analysis\":\"This is Problem E's Jacobi stencil. The baseline is valid on 4 cases, with mean runtime 0.06614 s (three samples: 0.06557–0.06693 s) and score 0.50 on a 4-core ARM64 target. No candidate measurements are present, so these are research hypotheses, not claimed gains. The source updates interior cells from four neighbors, stops only after a full iteration finds no change above 1e-5 or reaches the iteration limit, keeps initialized boundaries fixed, and prints every value with six decimals and a trailing space. Each objective must preserve those semantics for every valid input; the active-region proposal relies on the source's general initialization, not test-specific values.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"73211c9e51c941068d05ceb28393b09c\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"40733d785879d263e1ffc66992962bd8fde45b50b008634d85d368a534cb4715\",\"session_id\":\"c08531b8446a447bacb06c4500c0c033